          "paragraphs": [
            "We've woven this blanket in Bridgewater, Vermont, since 1931, on looms that were old when the mill bought them. It's 100% virgin wool, 720 g/m², whip-stitched at the edges by hand. It's the blanket that went out with the ski patrol in the fifties and it hasn't changed much, because it didn't need to.",
            "It's heavy, close to 2 kg for the queen size, and it wants a cold room. In a warm house it'll be too much, and moths like it as much as you will. Store it in cedar over summer."
          ],
